WEBVTT

00:00:00.255 --> 00:00:06.640
Kem cho, everyone! This is HeritageLens, our project for HackCult '26, Track 2.

00:00:06.655 --> 00:00:15.378
India's heritage lives in Gujarati and Hindi field journals, scanned PDFs and untagged photos, and almost none of it is searchable.

00:00:16.351 --> 00:00:26.377
HeritageLens turns that archive into one living atlas, covering all three pathways: regional text archives, an interactive map and 3D digital twins.

00:00:27.435 --> 00:00:30.441
Let's search for 'vav', Gujarati for stepwell.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:36.718
Results come from Gujarati, Hindi and English documents together, with the matching passages highlighted.

00:00:36.722 --> 00:00:44.282
Keyword, embedding and phonetic search are fused with Reciprocal Rank Fusion, so a place name matches in any script.

00:00:45.162 --> 00:00:54.109
Each document opens in a side-by-side reader: the original next to its English translation, with places and dates pulled out.

00:00:56.651 --> 00:01:06.410
OCR, IndicTrans2 translation and photo captions run on a free Colab GPU, and every translation is labelled with where it came from.

00:01:07.871 --> 00:01:14.655
The atlas puts heritage sites, Explorer Fellowship routes and geotagged photos on one interactive map.

00:01:17.887 --> 00:01:24.612
Journeys open in story mode, walking through an expedition stop by stop, with the notes collected on the way.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:36.636
Now my favourite part: 3D twins. This is Rani ki Vav in Patan, rebuilt from a photo as a point cloud of over 1.6 lakh points.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:44.197
One photo gives a Depth Anything relief; eight or more overlapping photos give a COLMAP and Gaussian-splat model.

00:01:45.352 --> 00:01:56.378
Anyone can contribute scans, PDFs, slides or photos. Each upload becomes small jobs: extract, OCR, translate, caption and index.

00:01:57.642 --> 00:02:07.757
The pipeline dashboard streams every job live. The server runs CPU jobs, and Colab GPUs pull GPU jobs over plain HTTPS.

00:02:07.772 --> 00:02:11.307
All 300 jobs in this archive have succeeded.

00:02:12.577 --> 00:02:24.287
The architecture: Next.js on Vercel, a stateless FastAPI service, and a durable job queue with CPU and GPU lanes, leases, retries and dead letters.

00:02:24.294 --> 00:02:34.706
To scale, just open more GPU notebooks; no open ports needed. Data lives in PostgreSQL with pgvector, or SQLite on a laptop.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:43.940
Quality matters: 318 automated tests, types shared from the API to the UI, and CI on every push.

00:02:44.246 --> 00:02:50.669
HeritageLens helps researchers, archivists and heritage tourism explore India's past, in any language.

00:02:50.872 --> 00:02:57.009
It's live at heritagelens-hc26.vercel.app. Thank you!
